\section{Current Underway Replay Baseline}
The current external-data baseline uses oceanography-waves-lib v1.4.0: a 28 ft estimated hull RAO at 5 kn, following seas northbound and head/bow-quartering seas southbound, both with a $\pm3^\circ$ heading sine every 20 s. Each case contains eight 1200 s, 200 Hz records. The final 900 s are scored, except AHRS attitude (final 60 s). Displacement and velocity truth are relative to the declared cruise track; total acceleration and delivered IMU samples are retained. These are deterministic regression measurements, not confidence intervals or sea trials.

